{1211}{37l	
2 January, 1721

Been exiled to this god-forsaken rock, sent away by some bloody human jury who couldn't judge which end of a mule was its backside.  Guess I shouldn't be all that surprised...no one ever accused humans of being very smart.  Looking back, maybe I shouldn't of hit that damned gnome so hard, but no one goes around insulting MY clan, and that's just the way of it.  By Alberich, I could use a little snuff...
}

{1212}{37l
4 September, 1721

Guess no one from the Wheel Clan heard about what happened to me.  My fault for going out without telling anyone where I was headed.  I suppose I didn't rightly know myself.  Just had to get away for a little while.  Now it looks like I'm stuck here until Loghaire decides I've been away too long.  And that might be a while, so I better get used to it here.

Found the schematic for the Kathorin Crystal Spectacles in my pack the other day.  Reminded me of home.  Better hold on to that one...I don't think I could find that damn entrance without wearing them, and I've been there a thousand times.  Damned dwarven ingenuity.
}

{1213}{37l
12 March, 1756

Been here a few years now...I can't believe it's been 35 years already.  I've been busy...figured I was going to have to live with all the degenerates on this island, so I broke a few noses and set myself up as the leader around here.  Recruited a big half-ogre named Ogdin Big Fists to make sure things stay that way.  It ain't the Wheel Clan, but I suppose it's tolerable until I can get myself off this rock.
}

{1214}{37l
22 June, 1810

Not much to tell.  Still waiting to get the hell out of here.  Left things to Ogdin back in the encampment, and I've been scouting the island for the last year or so.  Ran across a group of fairly disagreeable women up north.  Can't say I blame them...women get the worst of it here on the island.  Steered clear of them once I saw the size of the spears they were carrying.
}

{1215}{37l
17 July, 1811

Ran across a man today by the name of Maximillian.  Lives out in the wilderness, all by himself.  Doesn't talk much, which is saying a lot for a human.  Didn't seem like he wanted to be bothered, so I borrowed a little water from him and was on my way.  There's something that man's hiding...that much I know for sure.  Of course, aren't we all carrying something around on this damned island?
}

{1216}{37l
8 September, 1811

Back in the encampment.  Saw just about everything there is to see on this island, and I know now that there's no way off of here.  Even looked into getting that old wreck on Shades Beach working again...I don't know where the hell that thing comes from, but its old and its like nothing I've ever seen.  In the end, it had just been there too long to be of any use to anyone.

Looks like I'm here for the long haul.  Not another damned dwarf on this whole island, that much I know for sure.  Figured Loghaire would have noticed I'd been away for so long, but I'm sure he's got other things on his mind.  Oh well.  Guess this'll teach me to go around pickin' on gnomes...}

