mes/gamereplog.mes:
// Game reputations start at 1000

{1000}{Reputation example.}
{1001}{Member of the Thieves Underground. This enables you to buy from black market stores and get free information and leads on jobs from other members.}
{1002}{Member of the Clan Maug. As such, you are a sworn enemy of the Pollock Gang, and there is a fair chance that they will attack you on sight.}
{1003}{Member of the Pollock Gang. As such, you are a sworn enemy of the Clan Maug, and there is a fair chance that they will attack you on sight.}
{1004}{Enemy of the Clan Maug. Members of the Clan Maug will generally attack you on sight.}
{1005}{Master Healer. Since you were trained by Kal-N'driel in Quintarra, you are respected and admired there and favorably regarded in all other major cities.}
{1006}{Murderer of Kal-N'driel, the Healing Master. This act of infamy that has earned you hatred of all in Quintarra.}
{1007}{Killer of the beautiful Clarissa Shalmo, the Throwing Master of Caladon. This has earned you the disfavor of the guards of Caladon.}
{1008}{Pervert of Tarant. Your exhibitionist antics in Tarant have earned you the scorn of its citizens.} 
{1009}{Debtor to Gurin Rockharrow. You owe Gurin Rockharrow 5000 coins for gambling debts.}
{1010}{Deadbeat. You have defaulted on your gambling debt with Gurin Rockharrow.}
{1011}{Betrayer of Gilbert Bates. You will find the citizens of Tarant a bit less cordial toward you than they once were.}
{1012}{Bow Master of Arcanum. Your skill with a bow is unmatched.}
{1013}{Dodge Master of Arcanum. You have been trained by Adkin Chambers in Mastery of the Dodge.}
{1014}{Melee Master of Arcanum. Your skill in melee combat is supreme.}
{1015}{Throwing Master of Arcanum. Training with Clarissa Shalmo has made you the throwing Master.}
{1016}{Gambling Master of Arcanum.}
{1017}{Haggle Master of Arcanum. Your dealings with J.M. Morat have gained you the title of Haggle Master.}
{1018}{Persuasion Master of Arcanum. Your reputation for oratory and negotiation is legendary.}
{1019}{Repair Master of Arcanum. Your brilliance with technological things is widely acclaimed.}
{1020}{Firearms Master of Arcanum. Your skill with firearms is unmatched.}
{1021}{Master Locksmith of Arcanum. Your understanding of locking mechanisms is unsurpassed in Arcanum.}
{1022}{Trap Master of Arcanum. Surviving Daniel McPherson's training has earned you fame and recognition as a Master of arming and disarming traps.}
{1023}{Enemy of Qintarra.  You have become the sworn enemy of every elf in Qintarra.}
{1024}{Friend of the Molochean Hand}
{1025}{Butcher of Stillwater. You will find that most citizens of the larger cities of Arcanum will have a dislike of you.}
{1026}{Master of Conveyance. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1027}{Master of Divination. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1028}{Master of Air. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1029}{Master of Earth. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1030}{Master of Fire. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1031}{Master of Water. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1032}{Master of Force. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1033}{Master of Mental Magick. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1034}{Master of Meta Magick. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1035}{Master of Morph Magick. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1036}{Master of Nature. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1037}{Master of Black Necromancy. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1038}{Master of White Necromancy. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1039}{Master of Phantasm. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1040}{Master of Summoning. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1041}{Master of Temporal Magick. All spells from this college now require half of the normal effort to cast.}
{1042}{Champion of the Pit on the Isle of Despair.  By defeating all of the pit warriors, you have gained the reputation of being the most grizzled pit fighter of them all.}
{1043}{Instigator of the Orc Riots. You are now considered an enemy not only of Tarant, but Caladon as well. Perhaps more armor is called for.} 
{1044}{Honorary Ambassador to Tarant.  Because of your excellent performance in the negotiations for Caladon's membership in the Unified Kingdom, you are seen as a hero by many of Tarant's citizens.}
{1045}{Enemy of Tulla. You have brought the wrath of every citizen of Tulla upon yourself.}
{1046}{Enemy of T'sen-Ang. Should you enter T'sen-Ang again, you should be prepared for a violent end.}
{1047}{Savior of Bessie Toone. The people of Shrouded Hills have taken a liking to you as the person responsible for freeing the ghost of Bessie Toone.}
{1048}{Destroyer of the Dread Crystal Spider.  For killing the Dread Crystal Spider, you've become a hero in the eyes of the people of the Wheel Clan.}
{1049}{Hero of Shrouded Hills. Because of your heroic efforts in helping Doc Roberts stop the bank robbery, the people of Shrouded Hills are definitely friendlier to you than they once were.}
{1050}{Outlaw of Shrouded Hills. Everyone in Shrouded Hills is looking to kill you for robbing their bank.}
{1051}{Survivor of the crash of the I.F.S. Zephyr. Since selling your story to the Tarantian, it seems some people have begun to recognize you, for better or worse.}
{1052}{Killer of the Whytechurch Murderer. The people of Caladon have taken a liking to you for ridding their city of the dreaded murderer.}
{1053}{Rescuer of Thorvald. Because you have safely returned Thorvald to his clan, the dwarves of the Wheel Clan have taken a liking to you.}
{1054}{Hero of the Wheel Clan. As the person responsible for convincing Loghaire to return to the throne, you have become extremely well liked by members of the Wheel Clan.}
{1055}{Assassin of King Farad. As the killer of the beloved King of Caladon, you will find yourself in grave danger if you were to ever set foot in Caladon again.}
{1056}{Orator of Ashbury. Because of your rousing speech that enabled the townspeople of Ashbury to finally build their monument, you find the people there to be friendlier to you.}
{1057}{Thief of Shrouded Hills. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Shrouded Hills, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1058}{Thief of Tarant. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Tarant, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1059}{Thief of Ashbury. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Ashbury, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1060}{Thief of Black Root. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Black Root, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1061}{Thief of Caladon. Because of your repeated attempts to steal from the merchants of Caladon, the merchants and the guards there take a dim view of you and your activities.}
{1062}{Enemy of Shrouded Hills. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Shrouded Hills, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1063}{Enemy of Tarant. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Tarant, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1064}{Enemy of Ashbury. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Ashbury, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1065}{Enemy of Black Root. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Black Root, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1066}{Enemy of Caladon. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Caladon, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1067}{Enemy of Dernholm. Because of your cold hearted killing of guards and citizens in Dernholm, you will be attacked on sight if you return there.}
{1068}{Kerghan's Apprentice.  Because you have joined Kerghan, you are despised by most everyone.}
{1069}{Owner of the Bates Mansion. As the purchaser of the famed Bates Mansion, the people of Tarant have slightly more respect for you than they did before.}
{1070}{Liberator of Maug Maulman. Because you killed T'val Nor and broke the spell that was enslaving the Half Ogres of T'sen-Ang, you have earned their friendship, and the enemity of T'sen-Ang.}
{1071}{Winner of the Ancient Game.}
{1072}{Enemy of the Wheel Clan.  For admitting to the murder of Loghaire Thunder Stone, you have become the sworn enemy of every dwarf in the Wheel Clan.}
{1073}{The Most Honored Dialectician in the Known Universe.  Because you have convinced Kerghan to turn from his diabolical plan, you are seen as the most skilled negotiator in the history of Arcanum.}
{1074}{Companion of a Fair Lady. Because the Lady Druella has joined your party, you benefit from a temporary increase in your Beauty and Charisma when dealing with others.}
{1075}{Betrayer of Magnus Shale Fist.  Because you have betrayed the friendship of Magnus Shale Fist, you are his sworn enemy.}

mes/gametelegram.mes:
// This message file contains text to be used in game-supplied telegrams.
// Only the message line numbers 1000 or higher are valid
// Each new telegram begins on a multiple of 10, and can use up to 10
// lines, which must be consecutive. Each line appears in the telegram
// in one big paragraph, with the word STOP between each line
// The first two blocks, at 1000 and 1010, are reserved for UI use

{1000}{CLASS OF}
{1001}{SERVICE}
{1002}{Class A Good}
{1003}{Class B Fair}
{1004}{Class C Poor}
{1005}{Tarant Union}
{1006}{Telegraph}
{1007}{SYMBOLS}
{1008}{ST-Stop}
{1009}{ET-End}

{1010}{NR-No Response}
{1011}{NO RESPONSIBILITY is assumed by this Company, beyond the exercise of due diligence and good faith in the transmission of messages, but their best exertions of their own line, which is in the city of Tarant.}
{1012}{ STOP }

{1020}{Mr. Ristezze
}
{1021}{Enclosed are the items which you ordered:

Elven Amulet/third kingdom....300 gp
Silver Clan Ring..............150 gp
Firestone Band................400 gp

}
{1022}{Please contact us if any of these items are not satisfactory.}
{1023}{

Winston Schuyler
P. Schuyler & Sons
44 Devonshire Way
The City of Tarant}
{1030}{To P. Schuyler & Sons
}
{1031}{Please accept this telegram as my commitment for payment of the signet ring I had made for my son, Gilbert Bates.
}
{1032}{Payment has been wired as per your instructions.  I will arrive in Tarant in two weeks to pick up the ring.
}
{1033}{Sincerely,

Benjamin Bates}

{1040}{I have discovered something interesting concerning our "friends" with the strange amulets.}
{1041}{I am off to investigate my theories regarding them, please accept my humblest apologies on my inability to meet with you in Tarant.}
{1042}{I understand all of this must be a bit disconcerting, for both of you.  If you've questions concerning the Panarii religion, stop by any temple and speak with a priest.}
{1043}{I believe there is one in Tarant on the northern end of Lion's Head Circle.}
{1044}{When you have the means, travel to the village of Stillwater.}
{1045}{I will leave word with the InnKeeper at the Bleeding Rose Inn as to where you can find me.}
{1046}{Joachim}

{1050}{
Professor Thomas Eakins
Tarant University

}
{1051}{L'anamelach. This is bad news, indeed.}
{1052}{I have sent a copy of the Legend of T'erre d' V'nt, which should have all the information you may need to defeat the beast.}
{1053}{DO NOT attempt to fight the demon until you have read the information contained in this volume. To do so would insure a disastrous turn of events.}
{1054}{Good luck.}
{1055}{

Prof. Eakins}

